{"id":"granicus-1-517","platform":"granicus","body":"City Council","name":"Park and Activities Commission Meeting","date":"2021-02-16","time":"","canceled":false,"agenda_url":"https://rollinghillsestatesca.granicus.com/AgendaViewer.php?view_id=1&clip_id=517","minutes_url":"https://rollinghillsestatesca.granicus.com/MinutesViewer.php?view_id=1&clip_id=517&doc_id=10e7fdab-feec-11eb-81b1-0050569183fa","packet_url":"","clip_id":517,"view_id":1,"video_url":"https://rollinghillsestatesca.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=1&clip_id=517","transcript_url":"","mp4_url":"","mp3_url":"","agenda_text":"CITY OF\n\n  ROLLING HILLS ESTATES\n  4045 PALOS VERDES DRIVE NORTH • ROLLING HILLS ESTATES, CA 90274\n  TELEPHONE 310.377.1577 • FAX 310.377.4468\n  www.RollingHillsEstatesCa.gov\n\n  Regular Meeting Agenda\n  PARK AND ACTIVITIES COMMISSION\n\nTuesday, February 16, 2021  7:00 PM  Teleconference\n\nPursuant to the Governor's Executive Order N-29-20, Park and Activities Commission Members will be\nparticipating via teleconference.\n\n- Commission meeting videos are live-streamed on the City’s website at www.rhe.city and available for viewing.\n\n- Members of the public may listen to the meeting live by calling: (1-669-900-6833) from any phone, Meeting ID:\n974 5587 7944 , Meeting Password: 509425. (Please note you will not have the ability to speak using the call-in\noption from a phone line.)\n\n- Public correspondence may be emailed to Cynthia Morquecho, Community Services Supervisor at\ncynthiam@rollinghillsestatesca.gov. Emails received before 5:00 p.m. the night of the meeting will be forwarded\nto the Commission for their consideration and included as part of the record.\n\n- Members of the public may comment online using eComment on the “Meeting Agendas, Minutes & Videos”\npage of the City’s website (www.rhe.city/MeetingAgendas). Once the agenda is published, there will be an\n“eComment” button next to the linked agenda under \"Upcoming Events\". Follow this link to the City’s SpeakUp\npage. After you register, you may comment on any item on that particular agenda. These comments can be seen\nby the public, will be considered by the Commission and become part of the record.\n\n- Members of the public who wish to speak during this meeting may join the Zoom meeting by accessing the\nZoom app from a computer (downloaded at Zoom.com) or tablet or phone (downloaded in the App Store), by\nentering the following credentials: Meeting ID: 974 5587 7944, Meeting Password: 509425.\n\nMembers of the public who join the Zoom meeting will not have video, and may request to speak using the\nfollowing process: After joining the Zoom meeting, if you wish to speak, please select the \"raise hand\" option at\nthe lower portion of your screen. The Meeting Host will send you a chat message to identify which item on the\nagenda you would like to speak on and will unmute your mic at the appropriate time.\n\nAgenda reports and other disclosable public records relating to each agenda item are available on the City's\nwebsite under Meeting Agendas, Minutes & Videos at www.rhe.city.\n\nPARK AND ACTIVITIES COMMISSION  Page 1\n2/16/2021\nAmericans With Disabilities Act: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, if you require a disability-related\nmodification or accommodation to attend or participate in this meeting, including auxiliary aids or services, please call the\nCity Clerk's office at (310) 377-1577 at least 48 hours prior to the meeting.\n\fPark and Activities Commission  Regular Meeting Agenda  February 16, 2021\n\n1.  CALL MEETING TO ORDER\n\n2.  SALUTE TO THE FLAG\n\n3.  ROLL CALL\n\n4.  APPROVAL OF MINUTES\n\n  A.  PARK & ACTIVITIES  COMMISSION  MEETING  DRAFT  MINUTES  OF\n  JANUARY 27, 2021\n  Attachments: Draft Minutes\n\n5.  AUDIENCE ITEMS NOT ON THE AGENDA\n\n6.  BUSINESS ITEMS\n\n  A.  SPRING MOVIE NIGHT\n\n  Attachments: Staff Report\n\n  B.  ERNIE HOWLETT FIELD USAGE REVIEW\n\n  Attachments: Staff Report\n\n  C.  CAPITAL IMPROVEMENT PROJECT LIST\n\n  Attachments: Staff Report\n\n7.  COMMISSION ITEMS\n\n  A.  ADOPT-A-PARK (VERBAL REPORT)\n\n  B.  ROCKBLUFF  PARK  SUBCOMMITTEE  MEETING  UPDATE  (VERBAL\n  REPORT)\n  C.  MATTERS OF INTEREST (VERBAL REPORT)\n\n8.  STAFF ITEMS\n\n  A.  COVID-19 UPDATE (VERBAL REPORT)\n\n9.  MATTERS OF INFORMATION\n\nPARK AND ACTIVITIES COMMISSION  Page 2\n2/16/2021\nAmericans With Disabilities Act: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, if you require a disability-related\nmodification or accommodation to attend or participate in this meeting, including auxiliary aids or services, please call the\nCity Clerk's office at (310) 377-1577 at least 48 hours prior to the meeting.\n\fPark and Activities Commission  Regular Meeting Agenda  February 16, 2021\n\n  A.  CITY COUNCIL ACTIONS OF JANUARY 12, 2021\n\n  Attachments: Action Memo\n\n  B.  CITY COUNCIL ACTIONS OF JANUARY 12, 2021 SPECIAL MEETING\n\n  Attachments: Action Memo\n\n  C.  CITY COUNCIL ACTION OF JANUARY 26, 2021\n\n  Attachments: Action Memo\n\n10.  FUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\n\n  A.  RECREATION FEE REVIEW\n\n  B.  HIGHRIDGE PARK MURAL PROJECT\n\n  C.  MAYOR'S BREAKFAST RIDE\n\n11.  ADJOURNMENT\n  The next Park & Activities Commission meeting will be held on March 15, 2021 at 7:00 p.m.\n\nPARK AND ACTIVITIES COMMISSION  Page 3\n2/16/2021\nAmericans With Disabilities Act: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, if you require a disability-related\nmodification or accommodation to attend or participate in this meeting, including auxiliary aids or services, please call the\nCity Clerk's office at (310) 377-1577 at least 48 hours prior to the meeting.","minutes_text":"PK\u0003\u0004\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000v��z�\u0001\u0000\u0000�\u0007\u0000\u0000\u0013\u0000\b\u0002[Content_Types].xml �\u0004\u0002(�\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0